title HUNK24 — the Photos app resamples smoothly (bilinear)
prompt Read REMEMBER + the 1024-round itinerary and the six-seasons double-seat; take the next agent-doable Lindy-first crux-first lap; approve own design round; send each finished increment; STOP at custody gates.
think REMEMBER's latest lap is HUNK23 (exact 120 hue turn); the named next agent-doable cruxes are a general-angle hue rotation, a bilinear resampler, or another Season-A journey. Custody gates 2/3/4 (hardware buys, provisioning, keys) stay untouched — agent-doable work remains, so not gates-only.
think Lindy-first crux-first: the resampler family (HUNK9 nearest-up, HUNK22 area-down) is a durable, oft-used core; bilinear is the clean, integer-boundable crux that completes it — chosen over the general-angle hue rotation, which needs fixed-point trig tables and is the larger, riskier lap. Bilinear is the hardest *solvable* clean move, not the impossible one.
think The half-pixel-center map pos = S*((2n+1)*src - dst)/(2*dst) in fixed point (S=256) lands exactly on the integer pixel at identity size (zero fractional weight), which is the property that makes a same-size bilinear resize byte-identical — the anchor the whole witness rests on.
think Proven by the algebra it must obey: identity byte-identical, a solid color exact at any size (weights sum to exactly 256^2, no drift), a 2x1 [A,B] upscaled to [A,(A+B)/2,B] with the exact center average, alpha blending alongside the colors, purity, still-an-open-image round-trip, and EmptyImage/OutOfBounds refusals — reusing the family's own error names, minting none.
obs First build failed on a u64->i64 coercion in bilinear_pos; fixed by casting n to i64 before the arithmetic ((2*@as(i64,n)+1)) rather than casting a u64 subexpression.
obs tame_style_check passed GREEN yet its scan fixture does not cover image/ (noted since HUNK17); split the three compound invariant asserts (fx/fy range, blend bound) by hand to keep TAME discipline, matching HUNK17's tidy. Selftest compound asserts left to match the file's pervasive surrounding style.
